It is known that in the martensitic transformation, a set of coordinated atomic movements in the unit cells is necessary for a new phase to form [ 15 ]. Additionally, it is known that the addition of alloying elements and the formation of a solid solution ( i.e. , solubilization of such elements in the pre-existing phase) result in the deformation of the crystal lattice [ 33 ]. Therefore, during the martensitic transformation, it would be reasonable to compensate such deformation before initiating the atomic movements necessary to transform the austenite into martensite. This results in an increase in the total deformation energy that must be absorbed by the austenite for it to transform into martensite. This could be expressed by the following equation: 6 U t = U SS + U TM \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
